skills it routes to, and are deliberately\n87: absent here so each has exactly one place to change. The line is between plumbing and\n88: posture: how to dispatch is theirs, how to think while dispatching is ours.\n89: \n90: **The routing carve-out, added deliberately as the third widening.** *Selecting* a\n91: route stays Out. *Verifying wiring you changed, and what you may claim about it*, is\n92: In; it is an evidence obligation whose subject happens to be routing. `skill-hub-routing.md`\n93: is the one rule on this side of that line, and it carries no route-selection guidance:\n94: the mechanics stay in the skills, and the rule points at them. A fourth widening that\n95: admits selection itself would dissolve the boundary; this one does not.\n96: \n97: **The ask-surface carve-out, added as the fourth widening, on an operator decision that\n98: overrode a research refusal.** A four-iteration decision-test run returned *refuse* here:\n99: naming a question tool per runtime reads as the \"which command\" family, and the paragraph\n100: above pre-refuses a fourth widening that admits selection. The operator widened it anyway,\n101: and what follows is the narrowing that keeps the boundary standing. *Choosing between\n102: runtimes, agents, commands, models or flags* stays Out, unchanged. *Naming the surface that\n103: asks the operator a question, in the runtime you are already running in*, is In. That is not\n104: a selection, because nothing is being selected: the runtime is a given, and the rule records\n105: which of its surfaces carries an obligation the rule already imposes. `communication-handoff.md`\n106: is the one rule on this side of that line, its §5 is the only place a tool name appears, and\n107: it names only what this repository confirms. A fifth widening that let a rule pick between\n108: runtimes would be the dissolution this one avoids."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/REPO RULES.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1794526802804,"end":1794526803212}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794526803229,"sessionID":"ses_e2ddecfe0ffezASL7yi66CNWdG","part":{"partID":"prt_1d221ef43001iQQRVwQKzDoWn6","sessionID":"ses_e2ddecfe0ffezASL7yi66CNWdG","messageID":"msg_1d221dfbc001cBlNBAUw04CZ7Y","type":"tool","id":"call_1788be264b074d3d8580687a","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/tests/ci-router-vocabulary-reach.test.cjs"},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/tests/ci-router-vocabulary-reach.test.cjs, lines 1-146\n1: #!/usr/bin/env node\n2: // ╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗\n3: // ║ ci-router-vocabulary-reach.test: the reach gate ranks the shipped fleet   ║\n4: // ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝\n5: 'use strict';\n6: \n7: /**\n8:  * Proves the router reach check decides on the shipped fleet only. A private\n9:  * surface an operator links into the skills root can tie or beat a shipped hub\n10:  * on that one machine, and CI never sees it, so letting it fail the run made the\n11:  * gate's verdict depend on what a checkout happens to link. These cases drive the\n12:  * check against a stand-in advisor and assert three things: a private surface\n13:  * ranked ahead of the declaring hub is a non-failing note, a private surface\n14:  * cannot hide a shipped hub that really takes the phrase, and the private\n15:  * surface's id never reaches the output.\n16:  */\n17: \n18: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n19: // 1. IMPORTS\n20: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n21: \n22: const assert = require('node:assert/strict');\n23: const { spawnSync } = require('node:child_process');\n24: const fs = require('node:fs');\n25: const os = require('node:os');\n26: const path = require('node:path');\n27: \n28: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n29: // 2. PATHS AND CONSTANTS\n30: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n31: \n32: const REPO = path.resolve(__dirname, '..', '..', '..', '..', '..', '..');\n33: const CHECK = path.join(REPO, '.skilled', 'skills', 'sk-doc', 'sk-create-skill', 'scripts', 'ci-router-vocabulary-reach.cjs');\n34: const HUB = 'mcp-tooling';\n35: const RIVAL = 'sk-code';\n36: // Assembled at run time from the private-skill prefix, so this file names no\n37: // private skill. The id only has to look like one to the check.\n38: const PRIVATE_ID = ['local', 'fixture-surface'].join('-');\n39: const SPAWN_TIMEOUT_MS = 300000;\n40: \n41: assert.ok(fs.existsSync(CHECK), `reach check is missing: ${CHECK}`);\n42: \n43: // A stand-in advisor that answers every phrase with the ranking in its scenario\n44: // file, in the live envelope the check requires.\n45: const FAKE_ADVISOR = `'use strict';\n46: const fs = require('fs');\n47: const recommendations = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(process.env.REACH_TEST_SCENARIO, 'utf8'));\n48: process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify({\n49:   data: {\n50:     trustState: { state: 'live', generation: 7 },\n51:     effectiveThresholds: { confidenceThreshold: 0.8 },\n52:     recommendations,\n53:   },\n54: }));\n55: `;\n56: \n57: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n58: // 3. TEST HELPERS\n59: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n60: \n61: function runCheck(recommendations, extraArgs = []) {\n62:   const tmpDir = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), 'router-reach-'));\n63:   try {\n64:     const advisor = path.join(tmpDir, 'advisor.cjs');\n65:     const scenario = path.join(tmpDir, 'scenario.json');\n66:     fs.writeFileSync(advisor, FAKE_ADVISOR);\n67:     fs.writeFileSync(scenario, JSON.stringify(recommendations));\n68:     const env = { ...process.env, ROUTER_REACH_ADVISOR: advisor, REACH_TEST_SCENARIO: scenario };\n69:     delete env.CI;\n70:     return spawnSync(process.execPath, [CHECK, '--hub', HUB, ...extraArgs], {\n71:       cwd: REPO,\n72:       encoding: 'utf8',\n73:       env,\n74:       timeout: SPAWN_TIMEOUT_MS,\n75:     });\n76:   } finally {\n77:     fs.rmSync(tmpDir, { recursive: true, force: true });\n78:   }\n79: }\n80: \n81: function detail(result) {\n82:   return `status=${result.status} signal=${result.signal}\\n${result.stdout}\\n${result.stderr}`;\n83: }\n84: \n85: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n86: // 4. CASES\n87: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n88: \n89: // A private surface tying the declaring hub and sorted ahead of it is what an\n90: // operator's machine produced for two shipped phrases. It is noted, not failed.\n91: function testPrivateTieIsANote() {\n92:   const result = runCheck([\n93:     { skillId: PRIVATE_ID, confidence: 0.82 },\n94:     { skillId: HUB, confidence: 0.82 },\n95:   ]);\n96:   assert.equal(result.status, 0, `a private tie must not fail the run\\n${detail(result)}`);\n97:   assert.match(result.stdout, /RESULT: PASSED/, detail(result));\n98:   assert.match(result.stdout, /outranked=0,/, detail(result));\n99:   assert.match(result.stdout, /operator-local=[1-9]\\d*\\n/, detail(result));\n100:   assert.match(result.stdout, /note {7}.*operator-local=0\\.8200, mcp-tooling=0\\.8200/, detail(result));\n101:   assert.ok(!result.stdout.includes(PRIVATE_ID) && !result.stderr.includes(PRIVATE_ID), `the private id leaked\\n${detail(result)}`);\n102: }\n103: \n104: // The JSON report carries the same row kind and the same anonymity.\n105: function testPrivateTieInJson() {\n106:   const result = runCheck([\n107:     { skillId: PRIVATE_ID, confidence: 0.84 },\n108:     { skillId: HUB, confidence: 0.83 },\n109:   ], ['--json']);\n110:   assert.equal(result.status, 0, detail(result));\n111:   const report = JSON.parse(result.stdout);\n112:   const rows = report.flatMap((r) => r.unreachable);\n113:   assert.ok(rows.length > 0 && rows.every((u) => u.kind === 'operator-local'), detail(result));\n114:   assert.ok(!result.stdout.includes(PRIVATE_ID), `the private id leaked\\n${detail(result)}`);\n115: }\n116: \n117: // Dropping the private surface must not hide a shipped hub that really takes\n118: // the phrase: that is the defect the check exists to catch.\n119: function testPrivateSurfaceCannotMaskAShippedWinner() {\n120:   const result = runCheck([\n121:     { skillId: PRIVATE_ID, confidence: 0.9 },\n122:     { skillId: RIVAL, confidence: 0.85 },\n123:     { skillId: HUB, confidence: 0.82 },\n124:   ]);\n125:   assert.equal(result.status, 1, `a shipped winner must still fail the run\\n${detail(result)}`);\n126:   assert.match(result.stdout, /RESULT: FAILED/, detail(result));\n127:   assert.match(result.stdout, /outranked +\\S.* sk-code=0\\.8500, mcp-tooling=0\\.8200/, detail(result));\n128:   assert.ok(!result.stdout.includes(PRIVATE_ID), `the private id leaked\\n${detail(result)}`);\n129: }\n130: \n131: // A private surface ranked behind the declaring hub changes nothing.\n132: function testPrivateSurfaceBehindIsSilent() {\n133:   const result = runCheck([\n134:     { skillId: HUB, confidence: 0.9 },\n135:     { skillId: PRIVATE_ID, confidence: 0.85 },\n136:   ]);\n137:   assert.equal(result.status, 0, detail(result));\n138:   assert.match(result.stdout, /operator-local=0\\n/, detail(result));\n139: }\n140: \n141: testPrivateTieIsANote();\n142: testPrivateTieInJson();\n143: testPrivateSurfaceCannotMaskAShippedWinner();\n144: testPrivateSurfaceBehindIsSilent();\n145: \n146: console.log('[sk-doc] router reach shipped-fleet ranking passed');","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/tests/ci-router-vocabulary-reach.test.cjs, lines 1-146\n1: #!/usr/bin/env node\n2: // ╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗\n3: // ║ ci-router-vocabulary-reach.test: the reach gate ranks the shipped fleet   ║\n4: // ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝\n5: 'use strict';\n6: \n7: /**\n8:  * Proves the router reach check decides on the shipped fleet only. A private\n9:  * surface an operator links into the skills root can tie or beat a shipped hub\n10:  * on that one machine, and CI never sees it, so letting it fail the run made the\n11:  * gate's verdict depend on what a checkout happens to link. These cases drive the\n12:  * check against a stand-in advisor and assert three things: a private surface\n13:  * ranked ahead of the declaring hub is a non-failing note, a private surface\n14:  * cannot hide a shipped hub that really takes the phrase, and the private\n15:  * surface's id never reaches the output.\n16:  */\n17: \n18: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n19: // 1. IMPORTS\n20: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n21: \n22: const assert = require('node:assert/strict');\n23: const { spawnSync } = require('node:child_process');\n24: const fs = require('node:fs');\n25: const os = require('node:os');\n26: const path = require('node:path');\n27: \n28: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n29: // 2. PATHS AND CONSTANTS\n30: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n31: \n32: const REPO = path.resolve(__dirname, '..', '..', '..', '..', '..', '..');\n33: const CHECK = path.join(REPO, '.skilled', 'skills', 'sk-doc', 'sk-create-skill', 'scripts', 'ci-router-vocabulary-reach.cjs');\n34: const HUB = 'mcp-tooling';\n35: const RIVAL = 'sk-code';\n36: // Assembled at run time from the private-skill prefix, so this file names no\n37: // private skill. The id only has to look like one to the check.\n38: const PRIVATE_ID = ['local', 'fixture-surface'].join('-');\n39: const SPAWN_TIMEOUT_MS = 300000;\n40: \n41: assert.ok(fs.existsSync(CHECK), `reach check is missing: ${CHECK}`);\n42: \n43: // A stand-in advisor that answers every phrase with the ranking in its scenario\n44: // file, in the live envelope the check requires.\n45: const FAKE_ADVISOR = `'use strict';\n46: const fs = require('fs');\n47: const recommendations = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(process.env.REACH_TEST_SCENARIO, 'utf8'));\n48: process.stdout.write(JSON.stringify({\n49:   data: {\n50:     trustState: { state: 'live', generation: 7 },\n51:     effectiveThresholds: { confidenceThreshold: 0.8 },\n52:     recommendations,\n53:   },\n54: }));\n55: `;\n56: \n57: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n58: // 3. TEST HELPERS\n59: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n60: \n61: function runCheck(recommendations, extraArgs = []) {\n62:   const tmpDir = fs.mkdtempSync(path.join(os.tmpdir(), 'router-reach-'));\n63:   try {\n64:     const advisor = path.join(tmpDir, 'advisor.cjs');\n65:     const scenario = path.join(tmpDir, 'scenario.json');\n66:     fs.writeFileSync(advisor, FAKE_ADVISOR);\n67:     fs.writeFileSync(scenario, JSON.stringify(recommendations));\n68:     const env = { ...process.env, ROUTER_REACH_ADVISOR: advisor, REACH_TEST_SCENARIO: scenario };\n69:     delete env.CI;\n70:     return spawnSync(process.execPath, [CHECK, '--hub', HUB, ...extraArgs], {\n71:       cwd: REPO,\n72:       encoding: 'utf8',\n73:       env,\n74:       timeout: SPAWN_TIMEOUT_MS,\n75:     });\n76:   } finally {\n77:     fs.rmSync(tmpDir, { recursive: true, force: true });\n78:   }\n79: }\n80: \n81: function detail(result) {\n82:   return `status=${result.status} signal=${result.signal}\\n${result.stdout}\\n${result.stderr}`;\n83: }\n84: \n85: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n86: // 4. CASES\n87: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n88: \n89: // A private surface tying the declaring hub and sorted ahead of it is what an\n90: // operator's machine produced for two shipped phrases. It is noted, not failed.\n91: function testPrivateTieIsANote() {\n92:   const result = runCheck([\n93:     { skillId: PRIVATE_ID, confidence: 0.82 },\n94:     { skillId: HUB, confidence: 0.82 },\n95:   ]);\n96:   assert.equal(result.status, 0, `a private tie must not fail the run\\n${detail(result)}`);\n97:   assert.match(result.stdout, /RESULT: PASSED/, detail(result));\n98:   assert.match(result.stdout, /outranked=0,/, detail(result));\n99:   assert.match(result.stdout, /operator-local=[1-9]\\d*\\n/, detail(result));\n100:   assert.match(result.stdout, /note {7}.*operator-local=0\\.8200, mcp-tooling=0\\.8200/, detail(result));\n101:   assert.ok(!result.stdout.includes(PRIVATE_ID) && !result.stderr.includes(PRIVATE_ID), `the private id leaked\\n${detail(result)}`);\n102: }\n103: \n104: // The JSON report carries the same row kind and the same anonymity.\n105: function testPrivateTieInJson() {\n106:   const result = runCheck([\n107:     { skillId: PRIVATE_ID, confidence: 0.84 },\n108:     { skillId: HUB, confidence: 0.83 },\n109:   ], ['--json']);\n110:   assert.equal(result.status, 0, detail(result));\n111:   const report = JSON.parse(result.stdout);\n112:   const rows = report.flatMap((r) => r.unreachable);\n113:   assert.ok(rows.length > 0 && rows.every((u) => u.kind === 'operator-local'), detail(result));\n114:   assert.ok(!result.stdout.includes(PRIVATE_ID), `the private id leaked\\n${detail(result)}`);\n115: }\n116: \n117: // Dropping the private surface must not hide a shipped hub that really takes\n118: // the phrase: that is the defect the check exists to catch.\n119: function testPrivateSurfaceCannotMaskAShippedWinner() {\n120:   const result = runCheck([\n121:     { skillId: PRIVATE_ID, confidence: 0.9 },\n122:     { skillId: RIVAL, confidence: 0.85 },\n123:     { skillId: HUB, confidence: 0.82 },\n124:   ]);\n125:   assert.equal(result.status, 1, `a shipped winner must still fail the run\\n${detail(result)}`);\n126:   assert.match(result.stdout, /RESULT: FAILED/, detail(result));\n127:   assert.match(result.stdout, /outranked +\\S.* sk-code=0\\.8500, mcp-tooling=0\\.8200/, detail(result));\n128:   assert.ok(!result.stdout.includes(PRIVATE_ID), `the private id leaked\\n${detail(result)}`);\n129: }\n130: \n131: // A private surface ranked behind the declaring hub changes nothing.\n132: function testPrivateSurfaceBehindIsSilent() {\n133:   const result = runCheck([\n134:     { skillId: HUB, confidence: 0.9 },\n135:     { skillId: PRIVATE_ID, confidence: 0.85 },\n136:   ]);\n137:   assert.equal(result.status, 0, detail(result));\n138:   assert.match(result.stdout, /operator-local=0\\n/, detail(result));\n139: }\n140: \n141: testPrivateTieIsANote();\n142: testPrivateTieInJson();\n143: testPrivateSurfaceCannotMaskAShippedWinner();\n144: testPrivateSurfaceBehindIsSilent();\n145: \n146: console.log('[sk-doc] router reach shipped-fleet ranking passed');"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-skill/scripts/tests/ci-router-vocabulary-reach.test.cjs\"}"},"time":{"start":1794526801731,"end":1794526803229}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794526803478,"sessionID":"ses_e2ddecfe0ffezASL7yi66CNWdG","part":{"partID":"prt_1d221f199001XA3fb9TXIDGOZL","sessionID":"ses_e2ddecfe0ffezASL7yi66CNWdG","messageID":"msg_1d221dfbc001cBlNBAUw04CZ7Y","type":"tool","id":"call_3cedb3a4e5ed49bd8a542063","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/lookup-trigger-index.mjs --json --scoring-only -- \"add two cases through the stand-in advisor to the router vocabulary reach test\""},"output":"{\n  \"candidatePhraseCount\": 2601,\n  \"discardedTokens\": [\n    {\n      \"reason\": \"below-min-token-length\",\n      \"token\": \"in\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"reason\": \"below-min-token-length\",\n      \"token\": \"to\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"reason\": \"beyond-max-query-tokens\",\n      \"token\": \"vocabulary\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"reason\": \"beyond-max-query-tokens\",\n      \"token\": \"reach\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"reason\": \"beyond-max-query-tokens\",\n      \"token\": \"test\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"indexHash\": \"cac6622b1df8eae3cf5fe37681108fd2e890dfeb637c88211608313d0c4227cd\",\n  \"manifestHash\": \"c243be4138be26b030af5a965ddc587955809ebe6ccd694e69601c9e81a327a8\",\n  \"normalizedQuery\": \"add two cases through the stand in advisor to the router vocabulary reach test\",\n  \"results\": [],\n  \"schemaVersion\": 2,\n  \"specFolder\": null,\n  \"tokens\": [\n    \"add\",\n    \"two\",\n    \"cases\",\n    \"through\",\n    \"the\",\n    \"stand\",\n    \"advisor\",\n    \"router\"\n  ],\n  \"totalCandidates\": 0,\n  \"truncated\": false,\n  \"staleFallback\": {\n    \"available\": true,\n    \"files\": 232,\n    \"matches\": 0,\n    \"paths\": [],\n    \"truncated\": false\n  }\n}\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":1},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"candidatePhraseCount\": 2601,\n  \"discardedTokens\": [\n    {\n      \"reason\": \"below-min-token-length\",\n      \"token\": \"in\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"reason\": \"below-min-token-length\",\n      \"token\": \"to\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"reason\": \"beyond-max-query-tokens\",\n      \"token\": \"vocabulary\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"reason\": \"beyond-max-query-tokens\",\n      \"token\": \"reach\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"reason\": \"beyond-max-query-tokens\",\n      \"token\": \"test\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"indexHash\": \"cac6622b1df8eae3cf5fe37681108fd2e890dfeb637c88211608313d0c4227cd\",\n  \"manifestHash\": \"c243be4138be26b030af5a965ddc587955809ebe6ccd694e69601c9e81a327a8\",\n  \"normalizedQuery\": \"add two cases through the stand in advisor to the router vocabulary reach test\",\n  \"results\": [],\n  \"schemaVersion\": 2,\n  \"specFolder\": null,\n  \"tokens\": [\n    \"add\",\n    \"two\",\n    \"cases\",\n    \"through\",\n    \"the\",\n    \"stand\",\n    \"advisor\",\n    \"router\"\n  ],\n  \"totalCandidates\": 0,\n  \"truncated\": false,\n  \"staleFallback\": {\n    \"available\": true,\n    \"files\": 232,\n    \"matches\": 0,\n    \"paths\": [],\n    \"truncated\": false\n  }\n}\n"},{"type":"text","text":"Exit code: 1"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"node .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/retrieval/lookup-trigger-index.mjs --json --scoring-only -- \\\"add two cases through the stand-in advisor to the router vocabulary reach test\\\"\"}"},"time":{"start":1794526802329,"end":1794526803478}}}}
